      "content": "Using a needle on a large, painful, potentially infected area is extremely dangerous and can cause severe tissue damage or life-threatening complications. Even with a new needle, you cannot guarantee the equipment is truly sterile enough to handle deep tissue, and attempting to drain it yourself can push infection further into your bloodstream. Spending hundreds at a medical facility is far safer and much more effective than risking a major infection or needing emergency surgery later.",
      "source": "target",
